# Daily liturgy import for Evangelizae.
#
# Deliberately off the hour (minute 23) so this job never piles onto :00 with
# every other cron on the host.
#
# The exit code is the only failure signal: the container exits non-zero on any
# failure, and without an alert attached to that exit a dead scraper is
# indistinguishable from a quiet Tuesday. Point the alert at this log:
#   /var/log/evangelizae-scraper.log
#
# Install with:  crontab deploy/crontab.example
23 4 * * * cd /opt/evangelizae && docker compose run --rm scraper >> /var/log/evangelizae-scraper.log 2>&1

# The window already reaches 7 days backwards, so a missed day heals itself on
# the next successful run. That is recovery, not alerting: if the job fails
# repeatedly the document for today is never imported and /pt/liturgy serves
# 503. Alert on the exit code, do not rely on the lookbehind.
